---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Verification & estimation methodology"
  description="How Vetlas verifies providers, generates review themes and AI summaries, and computes expense estimates — with explicit minimum-sample gates."
  canonical="/methodology/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Methodology</h1>
      <p>
        How data gets onto Vetlas, how it is labelled, and when we allow ourselves to show
        estimates and summaries.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="doc mt-25 pb-1">
      <div class="doc-block" id="platform-ratings-method">
        <h2>Platform ratings & facility photos</h2>
        <p>Scores show an equal-weight arithmetic mean of the available 1–5 platform ratings, rounded to one decimal. Each platform contributes once; we keep the most recently checked snapshot. One source is labelled as one platform. Missing sources are excluded, never zero. We do not claim complete platform coverage.</p>
        <p>Counts remain attached to their original source. People may review on multiple sites, and Justdial may already combine ratings from across the web. The mean is a convenience comparison, not an independent reviewer average or a measure of medical quality. Reposted ratings and unverified clinic claims are excluded. Reddit discussion votes are not star ratings.</p>
        <p>Every static score links to its source and states when and how we observed it. Search-index snapshots can be old; checking a result does not establish that the platform score is current. Manually observed Google Maps scores are dated snapshots. When configured, the separate Places integration can replace a Google snapshot with its live score. We do not emit combined external ratings as schema.org aggregateRating.</p>
        <p>Each published facility has an original public-source photo matched to its listing or clinic website. Photo credits link to the source, and original image URLs and check dates are retained in the dataset. Photos are optimized for fast loading; their date may be older than our check date. Sources retain ownership. The optional Places integration requires a reviewed Place ID, displays supplied photographer credits, and does not persist API photos.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="badge" class="icon icon-lg" /> Verification logic</h2>
        <p>
          Every profile starts <strong>unverified</strong>. Verified badges appear only after a
          Vetlas team member has checked the evidence by hand, and show the exact date checked.
          Council registration numbers are never verified or displayed — credentials are listed
          exactly as stated, with the source.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="sparkle" class="icon icon-lg" /> Review themes & AI summaries</h2>
        <p>Public-review notes summarize a small, explicitly labelled selection of visible accounts and link to the source. They do not establish recurring themes, verified visits or medical outcomes. Reddit discussions remain attributed community anecdotes. First-party Vetlas reviews are separate; none have been published. Future recurring-theme analysis will require stored review evidence and a stated sample size.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="wallet" class="icon icon-lg" /> Expense estimates</h2>
        <p>Published consultation fees are separate from community reports of the total visit bill, which includes consultation, medicine, tests and treatment. Unknown and conflicting fees are excluded from listed-fee averages.</p>
        <p>Visitors can report ₹1–1,000, ₹1,001–2,500, ₹2,501–5,000, ₹5,001–10,000, ₹10,001–25,000 or ₹25,001+. An optional exact total must fall within the chosen range. The estimated mean uses exact totals where available and range midpoints otherwise. Open-ended votes without an exact amount count in the distribution but are excluded from the mean.</p>
        <p>Results show the number of contributing votes, exact bills and midpoint estimates. Fewer than 10 votes are labelled a small sample. These anonymous reports are unverified, can be affected by case mix and outliers, and are not a clinic quote or a city-wide average. Reports expire 365 days after submission; voters attest that the visit was within the past 12 months.</p>
        <p>Shared storage keeps one current vote per browser and facility. Updates replace an earlier vote and deletion removes it. Cookies can be cleared, so this is not unique-person verification. Daily network limits reduce repeat submissions. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy and retention →</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="pin" class="icon icon-lg" /> City publication gates</h2>
        <p>
          Indore is a public-source directory with 15 facilities. Wider rollout targets are: Tier 1 cities
          need <strong>≥30 vetted profiles</strong> (target 80–100), Tier 2 need
          <strong>≥15</strong> (target 40–50), Tier 3 need <strong>≥5</strong> (target 10–20).
          Other cities below the minimum stay noindexed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="search" class="icon icon-lg" /> Search & indexability</h2>
        <p>
          Combination pages (city × speciality) are indexed only with <strong>≥3 vetted
          providers</strong>; thin profiles are noindexed until they meet quality bars. URL
          structure is lowercase and hyphenated: <code>/{'{'}city{'}'}/</code>,
          <code>/{'{'}city{'}'}/{'{'}speciality{'}'}/</code>,
          <code>/{'{'}city{'}'}/{'{'}provider{'}'}/</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-block">
        <h2><Icon name="info" class="icon icon-lg" /> Zero dark patterns</h2>
        <p>
          No popups, no lead-capture walls, no sponsored listing cards, no fake urgency. If a
          number or claim isn't backed by data, we'd rather say <strong>"not available yet"</strong>
          than invent it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
